  "id": "COMPOUND:23096 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) may interact with CX-1, through a series of target relationships involving SNU-387. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple molecules, including Anolobine, Dendocarbin K, and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, all of which ultimately target CX-1. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a common intermediate in these pathways indicates a possible functional link between the quercetin derivative and CX-1, likely through a shared biological mechanism. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, reliable relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) may influence CX-1 through the activation or modulation of SNU-387, which in turn affects CX-1. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) to exert its biological effects via a multi-tiered mechanism involving SNU-387 and CX-1.",
